# Netlify rules. Copied into dist/ by Vite, so they apply to every deploy
# whatever the publish directory is set to. First match wins — the SPA
# fallback must stay last.

# The two proxies the Vite dev server provides locally (vite.config.ts).
# storage.medplum.com is CloudFront and sends no CORS headers, so the browser
# cannot read a document's bytes from it directly — without this rule the
# request falls through to the SPA fallback and returns 404.
/api/*            https://api.medplum.com/:splat       200
/storage-proxy/*  https://storage.medplum.com/:splat   200

# Client-side routing: /documents, /dashboard … are not files on disk.
# Without this, reloading any route other than / is a 404.
/*  /index.html  200
